# Keep LF everywhere, in the repo and in the working tree.
#
# Without this, Windows tooling rewrites files to CRLF and every line in the
# project shows as modified: one `git status` here listed 29 files with 5199
# insertions and 5199 deletions, and `git diff --ignore-all-space` was empty.
# Pure noise, and it buries real changes in review.
#
# It is not only cosmetic. The Dockerfiles use backslash line continuations,
# and a CRLF file puts a carriage return after each backslash, so the shell
# inside RUN can receive it as part of an argument -- `useradd: invalid user
# name 'app\r'` and similar. Everything these images run is Linux; LF is the
# correct ending for all of it, including on a Windows checkout.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary: never touch these.
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.pdf   binary
*.pptx  binary
*.docx  binary
*.npz   binary
*.npy   binary
*.pt    binary
*.pth   binary
*.zip   binary
*.dcm   binary
*.db    binary
